Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 19:40:54 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(security): address Bandit findings

- B307 (eval, Medium): replace eval() of the merit formula with a small
  AST-based evaluator that accepts only gpa, credits, numeric constants,
  + - * / and unary +/-, with length and complexity limits. Division by
  zero and non-finite scores raise ValueError. A formula rejected at the
  prompt is reported and the current formula is kept.
- B110 (try/except/pass, Low): load_results() catches only missing-file,
  OS, decoding and JSON errors, logs a warning and returns False instead
  of silently ignoring every exception.
- Add the post-fix Bandit report (no issues identified) and four
  subprocess-based security tests: a code-injection payload is not run,
  invalid formulas are rejected without crashing, and the default and a
  valid custom formula still give the expected scores.
